(760414, 79103, 11832, '<td valign="top">how did you get so little noise with the f717 in such low light. i mean, ive done some 10-30 sec exposures before at iso 100  and its really noisy.</td>', 'how did you get so little noise with the f717 in such low light. i mean, ive done some 10-30 sec exposures before at iso 100  and its really noisy.', '2004-06-12 02:47:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(760478, 79316, 6900, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to vote on this challenge, but I would have given this (another) 5.  The point of view is unusual, which works for me.  However, I can''t see the multi light sources.  I know they are there, but I have to work for it.  In terms of creating a nice picture, I love the tones and the composition.  As far as doing well at DPC - you can''t make the viewer work for it.  5 seconds - that''s all you have.  From the time the pic loads (and sometimes not all the way) til they press the button - 5 seconds. :)<br/> <br/>Good luck!</td>', 'I didn''t get to vote on this challenge, but I would have given this (another) 5.  The point of view is unusual, which works for me.  However, I can''t see the multi light sources.  I know they are there, but I have to work for it.  In terms of creating a nice picture, I love the tones and the composition.  As far as doing well at DPC - you can''t make the viewer work for it.  5 seconds - that''s all you have.  From the time the pic loads (and sometimes not all the way) til they press the button - 5 seconds. :) Good luck!', '2004-06-12 08:20:32.000000', NULL, 0),
